    aiContent: {
      difficulty: {
        easy: 'Makes banker drawing decisions based only on the first tableau. Ignores the second hand entirely.',
        medium: "Uses a 'Value Sum' approach. Adds the totals of the two player hands and makes a move that beats the average.",
        hard: "Applies a 'Weighted Expectation' algorithm. Decides whether to draw based on which move yields the highest expected value in chips across both tableaus.",
      },
      considerations: [
        "The Banker's agency is the core of the engine; the AI must evaluate the 'Player 1' and 'Player 2' draw indicators.",
        'Requires a ternary resolution state: Banker wins 2/2, 1/2, or 0/2 hands.',
      ],
